A big point in the late game similarity is also the fact that everybody 
is just, understandably, trying to have all intrinsics for the late 
game. Some of them are truly intrinsics and no trouble to have, while 
some other are only extrincsic and *really* usefull.

Typically, fire, cold, shock, poison resistance are alle intrinsic so no 
trouble with that. MR, reflection, drain resistance, stone resistance, 
free action can only be extrinsic.
[DR and SR are only available in Salsh'em]

So by the end game, you try to have ring of FA, cloak of MR, amulet of 
reflection and so on.

An idea might be the following : restrict the number of resistance you 
may have intrinsically. Typically, if at some point you have to choose 
between free action and fire resistance, the choice might be not so 
obvious and depend on the situation.

See, the thread that appear about Slash'em monks wearing cloak of MR and 
amulet of reflection but lacking the very important drain resistance 
(especially important in the Guild or similar level [due to wands of 
drain]). It had been advised several time to wear a DDSM (provides drain 
resistance) or even to switch amulet of reflection for amulet of drain 
resistance in such cases.

Having a small vital set of extrinsinc that everybody needs augmented by 
a larger set of convenient extrinsics that "just" make your life easier 
would be a mean to force player to makes choice (on the larger set). 
Having some classes gaining these as intrinsics (like the monk do for 
the fire/cold/shock resistance but far to late to be of any interest) 
and some other having no possibility to have them intrinsically could 
change, at least, the equipement of the late game.

